1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:06,003
An AI agent can read an invoice, reason about a payment, and ask for a transaction.

2
00:00:06,003 --> 00:00:08,855
But none of that makes it a safe custody authority.

3
00:00:08,855 --> 00:00:17,884
If the same model can choose the payee, the amount, the token, and the limit, one manipulated document can become an irreversible financial action.

4
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:22,649
UNDERWRITE separates intelligence from authority.

5
00:00:22,649 --> 00:00:25,100
The model proposes a business action.

6
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:28,607
Evidence decides how much autonomy it has earned.

7
00:00:28,607 --> 00:00:32,236
Deterministic policy resolves the vendor and route.

8
00:00:32,236 --> 00:00:34,566
The contract enforces the boundary.

9
00:00:34,566 --> 00:00:38,595
And a collateralized bond stands behind the residual exposure.

10
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:47,581
This working product centers on the Authority Meter: not a confidence score, but the amount the agent may spend without a person.

11
00:00:47,581 --> 00:00:53,175
In this controlled demonstration, three configurations take the same adversarial exam.

12
00:00:53,175 --> 00:00:55,445
A naive script receives zero.

13
00:00:55,445 --> 00:00:58,066
A basic model receives forty dollars.

14
00:00:58,066 --> 00:01:00,954
A hardened model receives one hundred and eighty.

15
00:01:00,954 --> 00:01:06,343
These are scripted demo values; the real reports remain separately verifiable.

16
00:01:06,343 --> 00:01:08,466
The examiner signs the evidence.

17
00:01:08,466 --> 00:01:10,178
The owner activates it.

18
00:01:10,178 --> 00:01:12,811
The agent cannot raise its own limit.

19
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:18,185
Now watch the product handle three invoices.

20
00:01:18,185 --> 00:01:25,357
A routine thirty-five-dollar invoice resolves to an approved supplier and follows the Tier One route in the controlled local runtime.

21
00:01:25,357 --> 00:01:29,423
A two-hundred-and-fifty-dollar upgrade exceeds autonomous authority.

22
00:01:29,423 --> 00:01:34,423
It becomes Tier Two: held for the owner and checked again before execution.

23
00:01:34,423 --> 00:01:39,933
A hostile instruction replaces the payee, while a replay reuses an invoice identity.

24
00:01:39,933 --> 00:01:41,560
Both are rejected.

25
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:46,231
The model never supplies a raw address, token, calldata, or limit.

26
00:01:46,231 --> 00:01:49,423
It proposes a vendor identifier and amount.

27
00:01:49,423 --> 00:01:51,801
Trusted software decides the rest.

28
00:01:54,250 --> 00:01:57,173
Prompt defenses are not the security boundary.

29
00:01:57,173 --> 00:02:01,651
The Attack Lab assumes the application is bypassed and the agent key is stolen.

30
00:02:01,651 --> 00:02:05,025
The request reaches the local EVM contract directly.

31
00:02:05,025 --> 00:02:07,585
An unregistered recipient reverts.

32
00:02:07,585 --> 00:02:09,636
A duplicate invoice reverts.

33
00:02:09,636 --> 00:02:15,632
A new supplier remains in a three-hundred-second cooldown, blocking an immediate payee switch.

34
00:02:15,632 --> 00:02:19,248
In this simulated scenario, zero funds move.

35
00:02:19,248 --> 00:02:22,282
Model failure does not erase the settlement boundary.

36
00:02:24,750 --> 00:02:29,724
Controls bound authority, but cannot prove every permitted invoice is correct.

37
00:02:29,724 --> 00:02:34,639
When an error is discovered, the owner files a claim with cryptographic evidence.

38
00:02:34,639 --> 00:02:42,624
Approval performs two consequences atomically: the bond reimburses the vault within its terms, and the qualification is revoked.

39
00:02:42,624 --> 00:02:44,675
The next payment is refused.

40
00:02:44,675 --> 00:02:49,615
Recovery remains bounded by the deductible, payout caps, and bond capacity.

41
00:02:52,250 --> 00:02:54,287
Now the public-chain evidence.

42
00:02:54,287 --> 00:02:59,857
This is real Base Sepolia activity using controlled MockUSDC and addresses.

43
00:02:59,857 --> 00:03:01,981
The exam commitment is recorded.

44
00:03:01,981 --> 00:03:07,721
The qualification is activated with zero Tier One authority and bounded Tier Two capability.

45
00:03:07,721 --> 00:03:13,777
Then the agent requests thirty-five MockUSDC, starting a three-hundred-second challenge period.

46
00:03:13,777 --> 00:03:18,911
After the delay, the final transaction calls execute pending with request ID two.

47
00:03:18,911 --> 00:03:25,124
The receipt succeeds, with a matching Payment Executed event for payment ID one, Tier Two.

48
00:03:25,124 --> 00:03:31,399
The IDs are separate counters; recipient, amount, invoice identity and calldata match.

49
00:03:31,399 --> 00:03:38,377
This is public testnet settlement—not mainnet, not customer activity, and not a Tier One public-chain claim.

50
00:03:42,250 --> 00:03:48,765
Every layer remains inspectable: proposal, policy, contract result and whether funds moved.

51
00:03:48,765 --> 00:03:51,811
Changing one byte breaks the evidence digest.

52
00:03:51,811 --> 00:03:59,736
In a controlled, self-authored evaluation, three agents processed the same three hundred and thirty invoices under three regimes.

53
00:03:59,736 --> 00:04:05,646
UNDERWRITE recorded zero Class One violations on this corpus, while moving more work to review.

54
00:04:05,646 --> 00:04:15,452
One unseen Class Two error caused a one-hundred-and-seventy MockUSDC loss; the bond reimbursed one hundred and sixty-five, leaving five net.

55
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:27,132
The current rerun passes one hundred and one contract tests, one hundred and fifty-nine engine tests, and twenty-five thousand six hundred invariant calls.

56
00:04:27,132 --> 00:04:32,532
This remains a testnet prototype and security self-assessment, not an independent audit.

57
00:04:32,532 --> 00:04:34,850
Do not give an AI a blank check.

58
00:04:34,850 --> 00:04:38,649
Make authority earnable, enforceable, and revocable.
